    content: "<section class=\"hero\"><div class=\"hero-inner\">\n<div class=\"price-badge\">From $640 round trip</div>\n<h1>Cheap Flights to <span>Doha</span></h1>\n<p>Doha blends Arabian tradition with ultramodern architecture — the Museum of Islamic Art, Souq Waqif, and the Pearl-Qatar define this sophisticated Gulf capital.</p>\n<div id=\"tpwl-search\"></div>\n</div></section>\n\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Quick Info</span><h2>Doha at a Glance</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ig\">\n<div class=\"ic\"><h3>Country</h3><div class=\"v\">Qatar</div></div>\n<div class=\"ic\"><h3>Region</h3><div class=\"v\">Middle East</div></div>\n<div class=\"ic\"><h3>Main Airport</h3><div class=\"v\">DOH</div></div>\n<div class=\"ic\"><h3>Avg. Fare</h3><div class=\"v\">$640</div></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Why Visit</span><h2>Why Doha Should Be Your Next Trip</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>Doha blends Arabian tradition with ultramodern architecture -- the Museum of Islamic Art designed by I.M. Pei, Souq Waqif restored as a traditional market, and the Pearl-Qatar artificial island define this sophisticated Gulf capital. Qatar's city is compact, safe, and increasingly cosmopolitan, with world-class museums like the National Museum of Qatar designed by Jean Nouvel, a thriving food scene from street-side shawarma to fine dining, and the desert inland sea just beyond the skyline. Doha hosted the 2022 FIFA World Cup.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Seasons</span><h2>Best Time to Visit Doha</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>November through March offers the best weather with pleasant 18-28 degrees C for outdoor activities at the Corniche and Katara Cultural Village. April-May and October are shoulder months. Summer (June-September) is extremely hot at 45 degrees C+ with lowest flight and hotel prices.</p></div>\n<div class=\"sp\">\n<div class=\"sp-c\"><div class=\"sp-label\">Low</div><div class=\"sp-val\">Nov-Mar</div><div class=\"sp-price\">$490</div></div>\n<div class=\"sp-c\"><div class=\"sp-label\">Shoulder</div><div class=\"sp-val\">Apr-May, Oct</div><div class=\"sp-price\">$640</div></div>\n<div class=\"sp-c\"><div class=\"sp-label\">High</div><div class=\"sp-val\">Jun-Sep</div><div class=\"sp-price\">$790</div></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Airlines</span><h2>Airlines Flying to Doha</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>Qatar Airways hub at Hamad International (DOH) connects 150+ destinations globally. Major carriers: British Airways, Lufthansa, Turkish Airlines, Emirates, Etihad, Air India, IndiGo, Oman Air, Kuwait Airways, Saudia, EgyptAir, Royal Jordanian. US carriers: American, Delta, United (seasonal). Budget: Flydubai, Wizz Air, SalamAir, Jazeera Airways, Air Arabia.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Airport</span><h2>Hamad International Airport (DOH)</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>Hamad International is 4 km south of central Doha, connected by Doha Metro Red Line (10 min, 2 QAR). World's best airport 2021-2023 (Skytrax) with indoor pool, spa, art installations (Lamp Bear, Cosmic), 40+ lounges, and 200+ retail/dining outlets. Transit hotel in terminal. Free Qatar Airways city tour for 5+ hour layovers.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Budget Tips</span><h2>Save Money in Doha</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>Metro is 2 QAR ($0.55) per ride with day pass 6 QAR. Museum of Islamic Art free entry. Souq Waqif street food 10-20 QAR. Katara Cultural Village free entry. Desert safaris book direct with local operators (50% cheaper than hotel concierge). Alcohol only in hotel bars - pre-drink at duty-free. Use Careem/Uber over Karwa taxis for fixed pricing.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Top Things to Do</span><h2>Best Things to Do in Doha</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p><strong>Museum of Islamic Art</strong> — I.M. Pei's geometric masterpiece on the Corniche, 1,400+ years of Islamic art across 3 continents. Free entry. <strong>Souq Waqif</strong> — Restored 19th-century market with spice alleys, falconry, shisha cafes, and evening atmosphere. <strong>The Pearl-Qatar</strong> — Mediterranean-style artificial island with marinas, luxury shopping, and waterfront dining. <strong>National Museum of Qatar</strong> — Jean Nouvel's desert rose architecture telling Qatar's story from geology to modernity. <strong>Katara Cultural Village</strong> — Amphitheater, galleries, beaches, and global cuisine festival venue.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Getting Around</span><h2>Getting Around Doha</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p><strong>Doha Metro:</strong> 3 lines (Red, Green, Gold), 76 km, 37 stations. Trains every 3-6 min. Red Line connects DOH airport to city center (Msheireb) in 10 min. Single ride 2 QAR, day pass 6 QAR, weekly 30 QAR. <strong>Karwa Taxis:</strong> Metered, turquoise livery. Flag fall 4 QAR, 1.6 QAR/km. App booking via Karwa app. <strong>Uber/Careem:</strong> Widely available, fixed pricing, English-speaking drivers. <strong>Car rental:</strong> Major brands at DOH and city. Right-hand drive, GPS essential. Avoid rush hours (7-9 AM, 4-7 PM).</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Where to Stay</span><h2>Where to Stay in Doha</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p><strong>West Bay (The Pearl, Lusail):</strong> Skyline hotels, business district, $150-400/night. <strong>Souq Waqif / Msheireb:</strong> Heritage boutique hotels, walking distance to market, $120-250/night. <strong>The Pearl-Qatar:</strong> Luxury marina residences, upscale dining, $250-500/night. <strong>Katara / Cultural Village:</strong> Beach access, arts district, $100-300/night. <strong>Al Sadd / Old Airport:</strong> Budget-friendly, local neighborhoods, $40-100/night. <strong>Airport transit:</strong> Oryx Airport Hotel inside DOH terminal for layovers.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">FAQ</span><h2>Frequently Asked Questions About Doha</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><div class=\"faq-item\"><h3>What is the best month to fly to Doha?</h3><p>November through March offers the best weather (18-28°C) but highest prices. For value, target April-May or October (shoulder season) with 25-35°C temperatures and 30-40% lower fares.</p></div><div class=\"faq-item\"><h3>Do I need a visa for Qatar?</h3><p>80+ nationalities get visa-free entry for 30-90 days (US, UK, EU, Canada, Australia, NZ, GCC). Check <a href=\"https://www.visitqatar.qa/plan-your-trip/visa\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hayya platform</a> for current rules. Visa on arrival available for many others.</p></div><div class=\"faq-item\"><h3>Is Doha expensive to visit?</h3><p>Doha can be expensive for luxury (5-star hotels $300+/night, fine dining $100+/meal) but budget-friendly options exist: Metro ($1/ride), street food ($3-8), free museums, mid-range hotels $80-150/night.</p></div><div class=\"faq-item\"><h3>What should I wear in Doha?</h3><p>Modest dress recommended: shoulders and knees covered in public. Swimwear only at hotel pools/beaches. Women don't need hijab but avoid revealing clothing. Men should avoid shorts in malls/museums.</p></div><div class=\"faq-item\"><h3>Can I drink alcohol in Doha?</h3><p>Alcohol served only in licensed hotel restaurants/bars and Qatar Distribution Company stores (residents only). Public intoxication illegal. No alcohol in World Cup stadiums (2022 rule).</p></div><div class=\"faq-item\"><h3>How many days do I need in Doha?</h3><p>3 days covers highlights (MIA, Souq Waqif, Pearl, Katara, National Museum). 5 days adds Inland Sea desert safari, day trip to Al Zubarah Fort (UNESCO), and relaxed pace.</p></div><div class=\"faq-item\"><h3>Is Doha safe for solo travelers?</h3><p>Yes — Qatar consistently ranks among world's safest countries. Low crime, visible police, women travel solo comfortably. Standard precautions apply (secure valuables, avoid isolated areas at night).</p></div></div>\n</section>\n<div id=\"tp-popular-destinations\"></div>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">FAQs</span><h2>How much does a round-trip flight to Doha cost?</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>Round-trip flights to Doha typically start from $600. Prices vary by season and departure city. Book November-March for the best deals. Budget carriers often offer fares 20-30% lower than full-service airlines.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">FAQs</span><h2>What is the best time of year to visit Doha?</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>The best time to visit Doha is November-March. During these months, the weather is pleasant and you will avoid peak tourist crowds. Book early for the best rates during these popular travel periods.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">FAQs</span><h2>Do I need a visa to visit Doha, Qatar?</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>Visa requirements for Qatar depend on your nationality. Many countries offer visa-free entry for short stays. Check the latest entry requirements on the official immigration website before booking, as policies can change.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">FAQs</span><h2>How many days should I spend in Doha?</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>A minimum of 4-5 days is recommended for Doha to explore the main attractions without rushing. For a more relaxed pace or to take day trips, plan for 7-10 days. Doha offers plenty to see and do for longer stays.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">FAQs</span><h2>Is Doha expensive for tourists?</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>Flights to Doha start from $600 round trip. Daily costs vary. Doha offers options for every budget. Budget travelers can expect to spend $50-80 per day, while mid-range travelers should budget $120-200 per day including accommodation, food, and activities.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Flights</span><h2>Popular Flights from Doha</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>Routes to Doha:\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/flight-routes/cairo-to-doha\">Cairo → Doha</a> — $310 round trip</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Explore more: <a href=\"/destinations/orlando\">Orlando</a>, <a href=\"/destinations/tokyo\">Tokyo</a>, <a href=\"/destinations/singapore\">Singapore</a>, and <a href=\"/destinations/london\">London</a>.</p> In the meantime, explore our most popular flight guides: <a href=\"/destinations/orlando\">Orlando</a>, <a href=\"/destinations/tokyo\">Tokyo</a>, <a href=\"/destinations/singapore\">Singapore</a>, and <a href=\"/destinations/london\">London</a>.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Explore</span><h2>Related Destinations</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\">\n    <ul>\n    <li><a href=\"/destinations/bali\">Bali</a> - Tropical island with rice terraces, temples, and surf breaks</li>\n    <li><a href=\"/destinations/cancun\">Cancun</a> - Caribbean beaches, Mayan ruins, and all-inclusive resorts</li>\n    <li><a href=\"/destinations/cape-town\">Cape Town</a> - Table Mountain, wine country, and African coastal beauty</li>\n    <li><a href=\"/destinations/dubai\">Dubai</a> - Futuristic skyscrapers and desert adventures in the UAE</li>\n    </ul>\n</div>\n</section>"
