    content: "<section class=\"hero\"><div class=\"hero-inner\">\n<div class=\"price-badge\">From $640 round trip</div>\n<h1>Cheap Flights to <span>Rio de Janeiro</span></h1>\n<p>Rio de Janeiro is a city of dramatic natural beauty — Sugarloaf Mountain, Christ the Redeemer, Copacabana, Ipanema, and Carnival define Brazil's most iconic city.</p>\n<div id=\"tpwl-search\"></div>\n</div></section>\n\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Quick Info</span><h2>Rio de Janeiro at a Glance</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ig\">\n<div class=\"ic\"><h3>Country</h3><div class=\"v\">Brazil</div></div>\n<div class=\"ic\"><h3>Region</h3><div class=\"v\">South America</div></div>\n<div class=\"ic\"><h3>Main Airport</h3><div class=\"v\">GIG</div></div>\n<div class=\"ic\"><h3>Avg. Fare</h3><div class=\"v\">$640</div></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Why Visit</span><h2>Why Rio de Janeiro Should Be Your Next Trip</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>Rio de Janeiro is a city of dramatic natural beauty -- Sugarloaf Mountain rising 396 meters from the bay, Christ the Redeemer atop Corcovado with arms outstretched over the city, and the curves of Copacabana and Ipanema beaches framed by lush green mountains. Brazil's most iconic city pulses with samba, Carnival's massive parade at the Sambodromo, and a joie de vivre that makes every day feel like a celebration. The city hosted the 2016 Olympics and remains the cultural capital of Brazil with a legendary nightlife scene.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Seasons</span><h2>Best Time to Visit Rio de Janeiro</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>December through March is summer with beach weather and Carnival in February/March -- the most popular and expensive time. April through June and October through November offer warm temperatures and fewer crowds. July through September is winter with mild 20-25 degrees C, lowest prices, and whale watching season.</p></div>\n<div class=\"sp\"><div class=\"sp-c\"><div class=\"sp-label\">Low Season</div><div class=\"sp-val\">May-Sep</div><div class=\"sp-price\">$520</div></div><div class=\"sp-c\"><div class=\"sp-label\">Shoulder</div><div class=\"sp-val\">Apr, Oct-Nov</div><div class=\"sp-price\">$640</div></div><div class=\"sp-c\"><div class=\"sp-label\">Peak</div><div class=\"sp-val\">Dec-Mar</div><div class=\"sp-price\">$890</div></div></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Airlines</span><h2>Airlines Flying to Rio de Janeiro</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>GOL and LATAM (hubs at GIG) dominate domestic Brazil. International: American, Delta, United from US; TAP Air Portugal, Air France, KLM, Lufthansa, British Airways, Iberia from Europe; Aerolineas Argentinas, Copa, Avianca from Latin America. Direct from US: Miami (AA, GOL), Atlanta (DL), Houston (UA), Newark (UA). Newark-Rio on United is only nonstop from NYC area.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Airport</span><h2>Galeao International Airport (GIG)</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>GIG is 20 km north of Copacabana. BRT TransCarioca to city center (45 min, 4.30 BRL). Uber: 60-100 BRL to Zona Sul. Official taxi: 120-180 BRL. Metro Line 2 connects to BRT at Vicente de Carvalho. Santos Dumont (SDU) 2 km from Centro handles domestic shuttles — convenient for Rio-Sao Paulo (bridge flights every 30 min).</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Budget Tips</span><h2>Save Money in Rio de Janeiro</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><ul class=\"it\"><li><strong>Metro + BRT:</strong> 4.30-7.50 BRL vs 30-50 BRL Uber across city</li><li><strong>Street food:</strong> Pastel, coxinha, acai bowls 10-25 BRL vs 80+ at beach kiosks</li><li><strong>Free attractions:</strong> Christ the Redeemer (train extra), Sugarloaf (hike up free), beaches, parks</li><li><strong>Carnival:</strong> Book 6+ months ahead or avoid — prices 3-5x normal</li><li><strong>Caipirinha:</strong> Buy cachaca + lime + sugar at market, make at Airbnb vs 35 BRL at bars</li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Top Things to Do</span><h2>Top Things to Do in Rio de Janeiro</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><ul class=\"it\"><li><strong>Christ the Redeemer (Cristo Redentor):</strong> 38m statue atop 710m Corcovado. Train (20 min) or van from Largo do Machado. Sunrise best for photos.</li><li><strong>Sugarloaf Mountain (Pao de Acucar):</strong> Two-stage cable car to 396m. Sunset iconic. Hike Morro da Urca trail (free, 1 hr) for budget option.</li><li><strong>Copacabana & Ipanema:</strong> World-famous 4km & 2km beaches. Posto 9 (Ipanema) for LGBTQ+ scene. Sunday car-free Atlantica Ave.</li><li><strong>Tijuca National Park:</strong> World's largest urban forest. Hike to Pico da Tijuca (1021m), waterfalls, monkeys, 30+ trails.</li><li><strong>Santa Teresa:</strong> Bohemian hilltop neighborhood, tram (bondinho), art studios, colonial mansions, Bar do Mineiro.</li><li><strong>Maracana Stadium:</strong> Temple of Brazilian football. Tour or catch Flamengo/Fluminense match.</li><li><strong>Selaron Steps (Escadaria Selaron):</strong> 215 tiles from 60+ countries, artist Jorge Selaron's life work.</li></ul></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Getting Around</span><h2>Getting Around Rio de Janeiro</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p><strong>Metro:</strong> 3 lines, 41 stations, 58 km. Line 1 (orange) serves Copacabana/Ipanema/Leblon. Line 2 (green) to Maracana. 5.70-7.50 BRL. 5 AM-midnight.</p><p><strong>BRT TransCarioca/TransOeste:</strong> Bus rapid transit linking GIG airport, Barra, Zona Oeste. 4.30 BRL. Connects to Metro at Vicente de Carvalho.</p><p><strong>Uber/99:</strong> Safe, affordable, English app. Base ~5 BRL + 2.50 BRL/km. Avoid unmarked taxis. 99 is Brazilian rival, often cheaper.</p><p><strong>Walking:</strong> Zona Sul (Copacabana to Leblon) flat and walkable. Avoid Centro at night. Don't walk beach after dark alone.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Where to Stay</span><h2>Where to Stay in Rio de Janeiro</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p><strong>Copacabana:</strong> Iconic beach, all budgets, touristy, $50-400/night. <strong>Ipanema/Leblon:</strong> Upscale, best restaurants, safer, $150-500/night. <strong>Botafogo/Flamengo:</strong> Value, local vibe, Sugarloaf views, $40-150/night. <strong>Santa Teresa:</strong> Boutique, artsy, hilltop, $80-300/night. <strong>Barra da Tijuca:</strong> Modern, long beach, malls, families, $80-250/night.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">FAQ</span><h2>Frequently Asked Questions About Rio de Janeiro</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><div class=\"faq-item\"><h3>Is Rio de Janeiro safe for tourists?</h3><p>Tourist zones (Zona Sul: Copacabana, Ipanema, Leblon, Botafogo) are heavily policed and safe day/night with normal precautions. Avoid favelas unless on guided tour. Don't walk beach after dark. No jewelry/phones visible. Uber at night. Centro safe day, avoid night.</p></div><div class=\"faq-item\"><h3>Do I need a visa for Brazil?</h3><p>US, Canada, Australia, Japan: visa-free 90 days (extendable to 180). EU, UK: visa-free 90 days. Check <a href=\"https://www.gov.br/mre/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Itamaraty</a> for current rules. Yellow fever vaccine recommended (not required) for Rio state.</p></div><div class=\"faq-item\"><h3>When is Carnival and should I go?</h3><p>Carnival 2026: Feb 13-17 (official). Book hotels 6-12 months ahead (prices 5x). Sambodromo tickets $100-2000. Street blocos (free parties) citywide. If not your scene, avoid Rio Carnival week — book elsewhere in Brazil.</p></div><div class=\"faq-item\"><h3>What's the best way to see Christ the Redeemer?</h3><p>Train from Cosme Velho (20 min, book online ahead). Van from Largo do Machado/Paineiras (cheaper, more frequent). Hike from Parque Lage (2 hr, free, steep). Go early (8 AM) or late (3 PM) for fewer crowds, better light.</p></div><div class=\"faq-item\"><h3>Can I use USD in Rio?</h3><p>No, only Brazilian Real (BRL). Exchange at banks (Banco do Brasil, Bradesco) or ATMs (Banco24Horas network). Avoid airport exchange (bad rates). Credit cards widely accepted. Pix (instant bank transfer) ubiquitous — ask vendors for QR code.</p></div><div class=\"faq-item\"><h3>How many days for Rio de Janeiro?</h3><p>4 days covers highlights (Christ, Sugarloaf, beaches, Santa Teresa, Tijuca). 6-7 days adds day trips: Buzios (2.5 hr), Ilha Grande (3 hr), Petropolis (1 hr), Paraty (4 hr).</p></div><div class=\"faq-item\"><h3>What's the weather like in Rio winter?</h3><p>June-September: 20-25°C days, 16-18°C nights, low humidity, minimal rain. Perfect for hiking, sightseeing. Beach possible midday. Whale watching (humpbacks) July-Oct. Lowest hotel/flight prices.</p></div></div>\n</section>\n<div id=\"tp-popular-destinations\"></div>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">FAQs</span><h2>How much does a round-trip flight to Rio de Janeiro cost?</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>Round-trip flights to Rio de Janeiro typically start from $680. Prices vary by season and departure city. Book May-September for the best deals. Budget carriers often offer fares 20-30% lower than full-service airlines.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">FAQs</span><h2>What is the best time of year to visit Rio de Janeiro?</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>The best time to visit Rio de Janeiro is May-September. During these months, the weather is pleasant and you will avoid peak tourist crowds. Book early for the best rates during these popular travel periods.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">FAQs</span><h2>Do I need a visa to visit Rio de Janeiro, Brazil?</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>Visa requirements for Brazil depend on your nationality. Many countries offer visa-free entry for short stays. Check the latest entry requirements on the official immigration website before booking, as policies can change.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">FAQs</span><h2>How many days should I spend in Rio de Janeiro?</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>A minimum of 4-5 days is recommended for Rio de Janeiro to explore the main attractions without rushing. For a more relaxed pace or to take day trips, plan for 7-10 days. Rio de Janeiro offers plenty to see and do for longer stays.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">FAQs</span><h2>Is Rio de Janeiro expensive for tourists?</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>Flights to Rio de Janeiro start from $680 round trip. Daily costs vary. Rio de Janeiro offers options for every budget. Budget travelers can expect to spend $50-80 per day, while mid-range travelers should budget $120-200 per day including accommodation, food, and activities.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Flights</span><h2>Popular Flights from Rio de Janeiro</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\"><p>We don't track routes to Rio de Janeiro yet. In the meantime, explore our most popular flight guides: <a href=\"/destinations/orlando\">Orlando</a>, <a href=\"/destinations/tokyo\">Tokyo</a>, <a href=\"/destinations/singapore\">Singapore</a>, and <a href=\"/destinations/london\">London</a>.</p></div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"section st-border\">\n<div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"tag\">Explore</span><h2>Related Destinations</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ct\">\n    <ul>\n    <li><a href=\"/destinations/bali\">Bali</a> - Tropical island with rice terraces, temples, and surf breaks</li>\n    <li><a href=\"/destinations/cancun\">Cancun</a> - Caribbean beaches, Mayan ruins, and all-inclusive resorts</li>\n    <li><a href=\"/destinations/cape-town\">Cape Town</a> - Table Mountain, wine country, and African coastal beauty</li>\n    <li><a href=\"/destinations/doha\">Doha</a> - Modern skyline meets traditional souqs in the Gulf</li>\n    </ul>\n</div>\n</section>"
